{{- /* Every cell comes from RepoView.cell, which decides the words for each
state in one place rather than once per column. A failed run and a repo nobody
has ever collected both say "not collected"; a signal nobody configured says
"not measured"; a measured signal with no baseline says "no baseline yet". None
of those branches lives here any more, which is why adding a signal is a
registry row rather than another arm of a template conditional.
The rule those words enforce is unchanged: a failed run came back with no
metrics, so every count on it is a Go zero rather than a measurement, and
printing them would claim the repo sits at 0.0% with every package tested. */}}
